---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ROUTES } from '../data/routes';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const page = ROUTES.about;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
>
  <article class="prose prose-theme prose-lg max-w-none">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I&apos;m <strong>Phillip Byram</strong>, a developer who likes building software that
      stays fast, readable, and easy to run. Most of my work sits somewhere
      between product engineering, internal tooling, and automation, with a
      bias toward clear interfaces and systems that do one job well.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm working on</h2>
    <p>
      Right now that includes this Astro site, <strong>Todoer</strong>, and
      <strong>Ralph</strong>. Those projects let me explore web application
      architecture, developer workflows, and AI-assisted tooling without adding
      unnecessary operational weight.
    </p>
    <p>
      I use the blog to write about the pieces worth keeping: implementation
      details, tradeoffs, and the small decisions that make software easier to
      maintain over time.
    </p>

    <h2>Stack &amp; tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>TypeScript for most application and tooling work</li>
      <li>Astro, Tailwind CSS, and MDX for content-focused web projects</li>
      <li>Bun, GitHub Actions, and cloud integrations when I need automation or delivery pipelines</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub is the best place to reach me: <a href={SITE.github}>PilHliP211</a>.
      If you want to talk about web apps, developer tooling, or AI-assisted
      workflows, I&apos;m happy to compare notes.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
